PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F437A1786429087
OL,3,CNational Eisteddfod to return to
OL,4,CCardiff in 2028
OL,6,FCardiff Council Cabinet Member for
OL,7,FCulture, Parks and Events, Cllr
OL,8,FJennifer Burke, added: "Hosting the
OL,9,FNational Eisteddfod is a fantastic
OL,10,Fopportunity to showcase Cardiff's
OL,11,Fcultural life in all its creative
OL,12,Fglory, as well as the city's
OL,13,Fcommitment to supporting the Welsh
OL,14,Flanguage.
OL,16,F"The festival brings people together
OL,17,Fthrough music, literature, arts and
OL,18,Fperformance, and we're excited to play
OL,19,Four part in making sure there's a warm
OL,20,Fwelcome for every single performer,
OL,21,Fcompetitor and visitor in 2028."
OL,26,@pD@XOUxD@AOU}D@`O]
